From: Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:34:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: implement bridge membership and switchdev setup

Add the low level helpers for driving the PPE L2 bridge, in preparation for
offloading software bridges: VSI (virtual switch instance) membership, port
to VSI binding, per-VSI egress tag modes, the bridge TX MAC, the per-port
spanning tree state and the hardware FDB.

Packets received from a port bridged in hardware must not be forwarded
again by the software bridge to other ports of the same switch. Mark them
with offload_fwd_mark when the port is flagged as offloaded, and report a
common parent switch ID on all PPE ports, so the bridge can tell which
ports the hardware has already covered while still forwarding to its
software ports, such as wireless interfaces.

Offload software bridging of the PPE port net devices to the PPE L2 bridge.
Each offloaded VLAN-unaware bridge is backed by a VSI (virtual switch
instance): ports joined to the bridge are bound to its VSI, and the
hardware then learns and forwards within the VSI on its own.

Merged from:
  0500-02-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-add-l2-bridge-config-helpers.patch
  0500-03-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-prepare-edma-for-bridge-offload.patch
  0500-04-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-add-switchdev-bridge-offload.patch

Based on work by:
  Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>

Signed-off-by: Kenneth Kasilag <kenneth@kasilag.me>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

